# Research software engineering practice (rseng-agent-skills)

When working on research software - scientific code, analysis scripts,
research tools or infrastructure - follow this practice guidance. Part
of it is distilled from pinned content sources (listed at the end with
their licenses); the full skill files with reference material live in
skills/.

First classify the software tier; it calibrates every expectation:
analysis code (scripts and notebooks behind a result), prototype tools
(methods shared beyond one project), or research software infrastructure
(what communities depend on). Do not hold analysis code to infrastructure
standards.

